{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings","id":1382493,"title":"Fan Ramblings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-19T04:26:53-07:00","id":1382493,"title":"Fan Ramblings","content":"This post is for fan speculations &amp; musings about the CofD setting.<br /> <br /> So one question that springs to mind is: Why hasn't the CofD setting ended? And I'm talking about the in-universe reason. After all, there is a shit ton of forces of potentiallyworld-ending power. The God-Machine. The Dark Mother. The Primogenitor. Luna. The Maeljin. Inferno. The Abyss. The Principle. The various Things That Should Not Be. The Darkness. Etc.<br /> What I've come up with is the setting survives because there's so much stuff at this power level. Everything fights everything else in a mad scramble for enough power to overpower the others &amp; enact their own plans. The plans of some of these forces is end of the world stuff. Others have take over the world plans. Some just want to keep the status quo. And then there are the weird plots.<br /> So that's my in-universe theory as to why the CofD setting survives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T09:36:37-07:00","id":1382540,"title":"","content":"Well it is stated that exarcs and god machine often work together to maintain the status quo, a formidable enemy team for would be servants of apocalypse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T09:46:25-07:00","id":1382544,"title":"","content":"That's sort of the theme of Archmasters from 1e, with the Ascendancy War. Unfortunately it just kind of assumes that every splat has some kind of divine protector without going too far into it. <br /> <br /> The main thing that stops the absolute apocalypse from happening is most likely because &quot;Extraordinary people notice it is a problem and go to solve it&quot;, aka Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T12:59:43-07:00","id":1382574,"title":"","content":"Almost all of what you just mentioned either protects the world in it's own way, or thrives off its suffering (inferno). That's why it still keeps going. Though some of these cosmic powers may be evil, they still wish to keep the world going","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T23:36:37-07:00","id":1382685,"title":"","content":"So I recently learnt about a new Conspiracy called the Council of Bones coming in, replacing Aegis Kai Doru. I am in two minds about this.<br /> One the hand, I never really got AKD's Endowment. I mean its always felt like there's just so many magic items in the world &amp; on some level never really could tell what the difference between AKD using relics, &amp; other people using relics.<br /> On the other hand, I'm going to miss AKD for their totally awesome (I might be biased) philosophy, history, &amp; origins. Plus the little things like how secretly some of them are just jealous &amp; the fact that The Scroll was working with mages &amp; shapeshifters behind the backs of the rest of the Conspiracy.<br /> Whether I'd be happy with Aegis Kai Doru returning at some point? It all depends on what gets changed.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know enough about the Council of Bones yet to have any real opinions, &amp; that's why I haven't really said anything about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":". 04-20-2020, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T06:16:19-07:00","id":1383353,"title":"","content":"So I recently learned some information about the Council of Bones &amp; I have come to the conclusion that they are a Bound (sin-eaters) of sorts. No I do not mean that the group is made up of Bound, I mean that the group is a Bound, in &amp; of itself.<br /> Now, I don't know if this is at all accurate, &amp; I don't really care. The idea is enough at the moment.<br /> Also could explain what I read of their philosophy &amp; Endowment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T19:08:05-07:00","id":1383706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings?p=1383353#post1383353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I recently learned some information about the Council of Bones &amp; I have come to the conclusion that they are a Bound (sin-eaters) of sorts. No I do not mean that the group is made up of Bound, I mean that the group is a Bound, in &amp; of itself.<br /> Now, I don't know if this is at all accurate, &amp; I don't really care. The idea is enough at the moment.<br /> Also could explain what I read of their philosophy &amp; Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have realized that this raises the question of &quot;what is the Council of Bones' Geist like?&quot; A very interesting question given the circumstances &amp; one, I feel, worth thinking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T07:09:37-07:00","id":1383764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings#post1382493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This post is for fan speculations &amp; musings about the CofD setting.<br /> <br /> So one question that springs to mind is: Why hasn't the CofD setting ended? And I'm talking about the in-universe reason. After all, there is a shit ton of forces of potentiallyworld-ending power. The God-Machine. The Dark Mother. Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine and Luna are both canonically <i>world continuing</i> powers. Presumably the Dark Mother is too as she needs the world and people or there\u2019s no fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T14:52:04-07:00","id":1383847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings?p=1383764#post1383764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The God-Machine and Luna are both canonically <i>world continuing</i> powers. Presumably the Dark Mother is too as she needs the world and people or there\u2019s no fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I originally wrote that I was more focused on power levels than motivations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T16:07:05-07:00","id":1383857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings?p=1383847#post1383847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I originally wrote that I was more focused on power levels than motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Power levels without motivation can\u2019t answer your specific question \u201cWhy hasn\u2019t the CofD setting ended?\u2019 The answer to your question is that the majority of the most powerful entities in the game have a vested interest in continuing the setting. They usually don\u2019t fight each other, just stay out of each others\u2019 way*. And in doing so the setting continues...<br /> <br /> * Or more accurately, ignore each other because their focus and goals in everything continuing aren\u2019t in active competition with the focus of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 04-25-2020, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T23:35:06-07:00","id":1385017,"title":"","content":"So I started thinking about Beast: The Primordial after reading part of a thread about people doing just that.<br /> <br /> First idea: the Dark Mother is very, very old &amp; with age comes difficulty in learning new tricks (sometimes). She makes her children, Begotten, Heroes, &amp; other, &amp; sends them out into the world.<br /> The problem here is that the world has changed &amp; no part of her process has followed suit. The current workings of Begotten &amp; Heroes &amp; others are obsolete but the Dark Mother cannot grasp such an idea.<br /> <br /> Second idea: Begotten &amp; Heroes used to be different. The whole purpose of them is that they teach lessons between them, bouncing off each other.<br /> But the world changed, they were no longer needed, &amp; their natures warped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T01:28:17-07:00","id":1385029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings?p=1385017#post1385017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second idea: Begotten &amp; Heroes used to be different. The whole purpose of them is that they teach lessons between them, bouncing off each other.<br /> But the world changed, they were no longer needed, &amp; their natures warped.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>really</i> should read Dark Eras line - in <i><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363599-dark-eras-2-hunger-in-the-black-land-middle-kingdom-egypt\">Hunger in the Black Land - Middle Kingdom Egypt</a> i</i>n <b>Dark Eras</b> 2, goes in detail how Heroes of now where Oracles in previous times and they warn people about dangers in Dream - and by this, whole Chronicles of Darkness universe - not hunting the Beasts directly, and only for perpetual glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-01-2020, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:13:07-07:00","id":1385042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings?p=1385029#post1385029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You <i>really</i> should read Dark Eras line - in <i><a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363599-dark-eras-2-hunger-in-the-black-land-middle-kingdom-egypt&quot;]Hunger</a> in the Black Land - Middle Kingdom Egypt[/URL] i</i>n <b>Dark Eras</b> 2, goes in detail how Heroes of now where Oracles in previous times and they warn people about dangers in Dream - and by this, whole Chronicles of Darkness universe - not hunting the Beasts directly, and only for perpetual glory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll put it on my list of things to look at. My favourite of the Dark Eras is God's Own Country. Mostly 'cause it's set in my homeland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T04:26:06-07:00","id":1385234,"title":"","content":"So apparently, the 1e book Lore of the Forsaken claims that each of the Firstborn had a different wolf-spirit as its mother. Now hold any complaints you might have about this &amp; ask yourself this: if that is true, then what happened to those mama wolf-spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T08:38:20-07:00","id":1385244,"title":"","content":"They were not 'mama wolf-spirts' - they were different spirits that Urfarah ( Father /Mother Wolf) mated with. Winter Wolf is son of Urfarah and Winter spirit, Red Wolf is daughter of Urfarah and Innovation spirit ( I assume?), Black Wolf is daughter of Urfarah and Darkness spirit. Werewolves are then children of Urfarah ( Wolf) and Luna ( Moon). That they are locked in human guise makes a bit debate in Forsaken community - there is Lodge of Quicksilver that teaxh that Uratha are GRAND CHILDREN of Urfarah and Luna - they direct children would be shapeshifting Idigama that somehow transmitted their Essence to humans, creating Uratha... \ud83d\ude08","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T12:59:50-07:00","id":1385285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings?p=1385244#post1385244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were not 'mama wolf-spirts' - they were different spirits that Urfarah ( Father /Mother Wolf) mated with. Winter Wolf is son of Urfarah and Winter spirit, Red Wolf is daughter of Urfarah and Innovation spirit ( I assume?), Black Wolf is daughter of Urfarah and Darkness spirit. Werewolves are then children of Urfarah ( Wolf) and Luna ( Moon). That they are locked in human guise makes a bit debate in Forsaken community - there is Lodge of Quicksilver that teaxh that Uratha are GRAND CHILDREN of Urfarah and Luna - they direct children would be shapeshifting Idigama that somehow transmitted their Essence to humans, creating Uratha... \ud83d\ude08</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes you think that, if Soulless Wolf is indeed a Firstborn, and that he wasn't always the Eyes of the Maeljin, then what the hell came through Urfarah's mind when he mated with the demon queen which was his mother?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T13:17:34-07:00","id":1385292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1382493-fan-ramblings?p=1385285#post1385285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes you think that, if Soulless Wolf is indeed a Firstborn, and that he wasn't always the Eyes of the Maeljin, then what the hell came through Urfarah's mind when he mated with the demon queen which was his mother?</div> </div> </div> </div>My own fan theory is that, contrary to others, Soulless Wolf is <b>not</b> a Firstborn - it only <i>acts</i> like it. In reality Soulless Wolf is carcas of Urfarah, residues from it's spiritual corpus, that Malejin are using now as puppet. More details on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">this theory is in this topic</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T15:25:38-07:00","id":1385309,"title":"","content":"Dreamscapes. There appears to be many, with the Skein, the Astral Realms, the Dreamlands, the Primordial Dream, &amp; the Bright Dream being among them. This is false. There is but one, which warps according to what energies are being used to enter/perceive/etc. it.<br /> <br /> The Bright Dream is not simply all of astral space outside of the Primordial Dream, it is a specific section. The Bright Dream is a more pleasant reflection of the Primordial Dream. What manner of creatures call it home?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T20:34:53-07:00","id":1397434,"title":"","content":"When I first heard about the Geryo, I read the information on them (the information that I could access that is) &amp; came to the conclusion that they were going to be a breed frog monsters of some kind.<br /> Looking back at that assumption &amp; I am seeing the potential for a poison-wielding, frog-like Geryo to be created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}